        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The average cost of a new roof in Utah typically ranges from $8,500 to $18,000 for a standard single-family home using traditional asphalt shingles. For larger homes, complex roof designs, or premium materials like metal, total costs can soar between $20,000 and $35,000+. Most local projects average around $4.00 to $8.00 per square foot\nfor a complete tear-off and replacement.",
